{
  "_readme": [
    "Prospect pedigree that survives graduation.",
    "Ranking lists drop a player the moment he graduates, so without this the model cannot tell a",
    "struggling former top-5 prospect from a struggling org filler. It gives young graduates a value",
    "floor that fades as their major-league sample grows.",
    "",
    "players — captured automatically on every build from the top-100 and team top-30 lists.",
    "          Best rank ever is kept and never downgraded. Do not hand-edit; it rebuilds itself.",
    "",
    "manual  — YOUR list, for players who graduated before tracking started (these will not appear",
    "          in players{} because they were already off the lists on the first build).",
    "          Either a grade or an exact rank:",
    "            \"Roman Anthony\": \"elite\"        -> treated like a top-5 prospect",
    "            \"Some Player\": \"strong\"         -> ~top 20",
    "            \"Some Player\": \"solid\"          -> ~top 50",
    "            \"Some Player\": \"fringe\"         -> ~top 90",
    "            \"Some Player\": { \"top100\": 3 }  -> exact rank if you know it",
    "",
    "The floor only ever RAISES a value, never lowers one, and only applies to young players with a",
    "small major-league sample. Check reports/graduates.md after a build to see exactly who moved and",
    "which young graduates still have no pedigree on file."
  ],
